WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.037 --> 00:00:00.930
- Hi, it's Rie.

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.840
Today, I've been challenged
to take a popular food

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.750
and make it fancy.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.350
Today's guest is Jordyn Jones.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.210
She's a popular singer, content creator,

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.400
and a huge fan of "Make It Fancy."

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.480
Let's see what I'm making fancy today.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.070
- Hey, Rie, it's Jordyn Jones.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:20.570
I'm so excited to be a guest
today on "Make It Fancy."

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.060
I'm obsessed with Jolly Ranchers,

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.500
so I'm gonna put you up to the test

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.720
to make Jolly Ranchers fancy.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.420
The blue raspberry Jolly
Ranchers are my favorite.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.830
I cannot wait to go taste test soon,

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.783
and meet you, and make it fancy!

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.130
Jolly Rancher.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.090
I have had this before.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.560
I actually made a video.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.580
I made a cream cookie

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.310
and I used the Jolly Rancher.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:48.160
It's colorful and has a different flavor.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:52.280
It's very versatile ingredient for baking.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.000
Very strong aroma.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.130
I'm always confused about
blue raspberry flavor

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.500
because raspberry, it's not blue.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.150
There is watermelon, green apple,

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.800
blue raspberry, cherry.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.300
Does it taste like watermelon?

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.363
Oh, yeah.

00:01:09.363 --> 00:01:12.600
Sweeter, intense version of watermelon.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.600
I ought to do grape.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.034
Tastes like a grape candy.

00:01:17.034 --> 00:01:18.810
It is a grape candy (chuckles).

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:19.890
These are very cool,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.550
so I think I can make extra special today,

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:26.202
and as always, I'm
excited to make it fancy.

00:01:26.202 --> 00:01:28.150
(jovial music)

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.610
Right, here's what I got:

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.187
strawberries, pears...

00:01:31.187 --> 00:01:32.960
There are a bunch of pears.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.390
Bear with me.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:35.360
Pear with me.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.280
Heavy cream, butter, eggs, and buttermilk.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.420
From the pantry, I got vanilla extract,

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.910
baking soda, corn syrup, sugar,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.360
flour, vegetable oil, salt,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.090
white chocolate, and vodka.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.593
All right, let's get started.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:54.293
Make it fancy.

00:01:54.293 --> 00:01:56.710
(intriguing music)

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.470
We have cherry-flavored Jolly Rancher.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:04.140
Heat it in a pot, and melt completely.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.751
- [Producer] Can you guess
when they were invented?

00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:10.773
- 1940s.

00:02:10.773 --> 00:02:11.750
- [Producer] 1949.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:12.583
- 1949.

00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:14.770
- [Producer] Rie, how are
you so good at history?

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:18.230
- I watch a lot of "Drunk History,"

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.920
and it's a cherry very informative show.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:24.170
Once you don't see any visible candy bits,

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.070
I'm adding vodka,

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.123
and it's a lot of vodka: one cup.

00:02:28.991 --> 00:02:30.578
(light up-tempo music)

00:02:30.578 --> 00:02:32.420
(steam hisses)

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.140
All the Jolly Rancher
is melted into vodka.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.230
Take off from the heat.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.840
And cool-down, it takes about 15 minutes.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.390
I'm adding one pound strawberry in a pot,

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.970
half cup of sugar.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.010
You cook this until softened.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.200
Mix it up.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.110
It will take about 10 minutes,

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.130
but you don't want to burn on the bottom,

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.320
so constantly mixing.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.560
Strawberry is cooked, nice and soft.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.070
Transfer this in a blender.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:03.300
Puree the strawberry and
sugar mixture in a blender.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.360
Strain so it's nice and smooth,

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.260
adding Jolly Rancher vodka syrup.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.760
Make it in total, two cups.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.020
Next step, I'm going to
use four gelatin sheets.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:18.220
Cover with cold water to bloom.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:21.700
Make sure submerged completely.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.440
And while it's blooming,

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.550
heat up vodka strawberry
Jolly Rancher puree.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:28.620
I like this smell.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.950
It's fresh strawberry,

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.640
it's not smell too artificial.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.800
Sometimes, especially cherry flavor,

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.410
smell like a cough syrup.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:41.960
Gelatin is soft and almost
look like a jellyfish.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.450
Add this into my puree.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.710
Whisk it, make sure it
completely dissolved.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.570
Transfer to this pan.

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.060
Let is cool for room temperature,

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.810
and put it in a refrigerator.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.610
Chill it about two to
four hours, until it sets.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:02.700
So I have 25 Jolly Rancher.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.230
Put it in the food processor.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.390
Makes very unpleasant sound,

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.839
so hold your ears.

00:04:08.839 --> 00:04:11.370
(blender whirs)
Ah!

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.530
Am I breaking this?

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.390
(blender whirs)

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:16.000
Shake it off.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.440
And I just want to use
this big, pebble-sized one.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.920
It's kind of like
old-timey looking for gold.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.250
You are scooping gold from the sand.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.910
So I'm gonna set this aside,

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.430
but we have plenty more things to do.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:34.654
Using one stick of
room-temperature butter,

00:04:34.654 --> 00:04:36.053
just whip it nicely.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.023
200 gram of sugar, cream until fluffy.

00:04:44.371 --> 00:04:49.371
I have three egg whites that
I am adding little by little,

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:54.050
scraping side of the bowl so
everything is mixed nicely.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.670
Combine dry ingredients:
200 gram of flour,

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:01.600
1 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda,

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.440
half teaspoon of salt.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.550
Lightly mix.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.510
I have five ounces buttermilk,

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.970
quarter cup of vegetable oil,

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.360
one teaspoon vanilla extract.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.490
So combine together,

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:16.330
and I'm going to alternate dry ingredients

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.713
and wet ingredients.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.700
So everything is well-combined.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.513
Add this Jolly Rancher pebbles.

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:29.050
It kind of squeak like a dinosaur.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:33.051
Maybe that's just my hallucinating.

00:05:33.051 --> 00:05:35.030
(Rie and producer laugh)

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.640
Sometimes I don't remember if it was dream

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.970
or if it's really happened to me.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:42.720
Adding in a cake pan,

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.600
bake this cake in oven, 350 degree,

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.830
about 20 to 25 minutes.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.610
Do the toothpick test,

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.820
and when toothpick comes
out clean, it's ready.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:55.220
Bloom gelatin, two sheets.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:06:00.220
Cover with cold water, 1
1/4 cup of heavy cream,

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.680
three tablespoon of corn syrup,

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.040
two teaspoon of vanilla.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.930
Bring to simmer.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:11.286
- [Produce] Do you feel
like a lot of the audience

00:06:11.286 --> 00:06:12.619
is still making these?

00:06:12.619 --> 00:06:14.100
- I don't think so.
(producer laughs)

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.250
I saw a lot of people making
first Lunchable episode,

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.330
Stove Top stuffing.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:23.170
Brownie mix episode, I made a Swiss roll,

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:27.450
but I haven't seen people
made mirror glaze cake

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.560
for Eugene.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.990
I think this one is also difficult too.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.800
Came to a simmer.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.170
Gelatin's melted, so I'm
adding the white chocolate.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.980
Couverture chocolate has more cocoa butter

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.890
and melts more smoothly and evenly.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:43.300
White chocolate is melted.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.340
Take from the heat.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.050
Add in the two cup of cold heavy cream,

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.650
and gently stir.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:52.090
Cool down this to room temperature,

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.780
and put in a refrigerator,

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.760
and cool down about two hours.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.580
Two hours later...

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.190
White chocolate mousse is
set in the refrigerator,

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:05.610
and I'm going to whip this until
it look like whipped cream.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.020
I want to eat this.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.450
Looks very good.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:09.640
We use a good chocolate,

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:12.850
so I think this is a very nice texture.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.143
This is ready.

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:16.723
Yes!

00:07:16.723 --> 00:07:19.830
So I want to make sure the cake is flat,

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:23.480
so I'm going to cut a
little bit domey part

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.490
so it sits better.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:27.310
- [Producer] Oh, wow!
Very nice.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:28.990
- Smells good, too.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.250
Smells very fruity.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.720
Use this bowl.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.910
It is the same size as my mold,

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:38.530
so I want to use this as a guide.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.313
Jelly is completely set.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:44.893
Still there.

00:07:44.893 --> 00:07:48.930
Okay, so when you are
un-molding something very sticky

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:51.320
like jelly or pudding,

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.973
you hold it and spin yourself.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.046
No.

00:07:57.046 --> 00:07:58.792
(Rie and producer laugh)

00:07:58.792 --> 00:08:00.010
No, it should work

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.340
'cause I've done that before.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.549
(bright music)

00:08:04.549 --> 00:08:05.861
Oh, I'm so dizzy!

00:08:05.861 --> 00:08:09.013
(Rie and producer laugh)

00:08:09.013 --> 00:08:09.846
Oh, no.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.280
Yes!

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.490
And I have a glass bowl,
lined with plastic.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:18.553
Add mousse, about 1/3.

00:08:20.165 --> 00:08:23.510
So I'm going to use a
little bit smaller bowl

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:26.030
as a guide for the jelly.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.030
And add mousse,

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:31.030
probably half height of the bowl.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.940
Add the jelly.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.770
Add more mousse.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.380
Thick on the layer, it's done.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:39.180
Top with Jolly Rancher fruitcake.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.310
Tuck it in.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:43.250
Freeze this six hours, to overnight,

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.550
but we have tub freezer,

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:47.460
and that saves some time.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.410
One cup of sugar,

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.340
two cup of water,

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:53.960
and 10 Jolly Rancher.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:57.290
It's a blue raspberry
flavor, Jordyn's favorite.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:58.670
Cook over medium heat

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:02.280
and until Jolly Rancher is fully melted.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:06.770
While it is cooking, I'm
going to slice some pears.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.506
I'm using mandoline

00:09:08.506 --> 00:09:11.740
'cause you can slice it even thickness

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:13.160
and very thin,

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.290
but mandoline is one of the
most dangerous kitchen tool.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:20.280
I have cut my finger
before, so be careful.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.000
Hold object like this, not like this

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.097
because you're gonna slice your finger,

00:09:26.097 --> 00:09:28.040
and I think finger has more nerves,

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.440
so it's more painful.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.260
And once it's getting difficult to hold,

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:36.180
I use kitchen towel so it
doesn't injure my finger.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.800
I want to use just the middle portion,

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.340
where it just look like a slice of pear,

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.683
and I'm slicing two of them.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:52.170
So you want to pick
through nice-looking part.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.600
Those are all kind of cute.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.350
I didn't cut my finger.

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:58.240
Oh, this kind of makes
me want to go vacation,

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.008
like clear, blue ocean.

00:10:00.008 --> 00:10:02.000
(Rie laughs)

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.400
I want to swim in this.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.960
Jolly Rancher is completely melted,

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:11.290
and I'm going to cook pears in this syrup,

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.470
about 15 minutes or until translucent.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.640
So pretty.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:18.630
It soaked up all the Jolly Rancher color.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:22.040
Do the same process
with grapes, watermelon,

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.510
and green apple Jolly Rancher flavor,

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:28.240
and make Jolly Rancher-soaked pears.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.550
Dry and remove extra moisture.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:35.760
Put the piece of paper towel over.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.630
Put this in a silicone baking mat.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:41.530
Bake this at 200 degree, about two hours.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.100
And moving on to the next step.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:46.280
We have Jolly Rancher mousse cake.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.080
Remove plastic.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.140
And I have hot water here,

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:54.030
so frozen cake release easily.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.923
Remove the mold.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.100
And I have Jolly Rancher-soaked pears,

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.280
and I'm going to decorate.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:05.950
And I'm using simple
syrup to the cake part.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:08.370
It will stick a little better.

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:13.370
And you want to stick these
pears, over-wrapping each other.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.360
It is beautiful!

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.370
I'm so happy how it's turned out.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.750
It's almost look like a stained glass.

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:22.840
When you are just free-styling,

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:26.170
just think about balance of the color,

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:28.490
and if it doesn't stick together,

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:32.923
you can use simple syrup,
and glue to the cake.

00:11:32.923 --> 00:11:34.730
This is kind of look like a pickle.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.440
We're gonna heavy on the blue color

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.540
since it's her favorite.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:42.930
Once you come to this mousse part,

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.120
it is already wet, so
it's very easy to stick.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.881
And we are done!

00:11:47.881 --> 00:11:50.714
(whimsical music)

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.320
Jolly Rancher pear
mousse cake, very fancy.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.612
Let's see what Jordyn thinks.

00:12:02.612 --> 00:12:05.180
(cheerful music)

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:06.339
Hi!

00:12:06.339 --> 00:12:07.800
- Oh, my gosh!

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:08.810
You're real!

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:12.871
- I made Jolly Rancher
mousse cake for you.

00:12:12.871 --> 00:12:13.704
(Rie laughs)

00:12:13.704 --> 00:12:15.630
- I'm not watching from
my phone right now.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:16.463
- Yeah!
Wow!

00:12:16.463 --> 00:12:18.560
- When was the first episode?

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:19.760
- Like a long time ago.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.593
- Oh, wow!

00:12:20.593 --> 00:12:22.560
- But now, I am like,

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.990
there's an episode that
drops, I'm the first view.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:26.560
How Would You Make It Fancy fan.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.170
- You are over 21, right?

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:29.020
- I am.
Okay.

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:29.853
(Rie laughs)

00:12:29.853 --> 00:12:31.330
- I am.
(Rie laughs)

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.427
I don't drink, though.
- Okay.

00:12:32.427 --> 00:12:33.812
- But I know how you are.

00:12:33.812 --> 00:12:35.550
(Rie and Jordyn laugh)

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.383
- You're a true fan.

00:12:36.383 --> 00:12:37.980
And when I made this cake,

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.701
I didn't think about cutting it.

00:12:39.701 --> 00:12:40.729
(Jordyn laughs)

00:12:40.729 --> 00:12:43.400
So, I might struggle.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:44.770
- We're here for it.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.670
It looks beautiful!
- Just for you!

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:47.600
- Wow!

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.767
- [Rie and Jordyn] Cheers!

00:12:51.131 --> 00:12:51.964
- Mm.

00:12:51.964 --> 00:12:52.797
- Mm...

00:12:53.723 --> 00:12:55.283
Mm...
- Mm.

00:12:55.283 --> 00:12:56.340
- Mm...

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.810
- That is the blue raspberry you like.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.200
- Yes!

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:01.249
You made them fancy.

00:13:01.249 --> 00:13:02.500
- Yay!

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:05.310
If I ask you to dance,

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.170
can you make a special dance for us?

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:08.330
- Oh, my God, yes!
(Rie laughs)

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:09.433
So you we can do like,

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:11.981
make it fancy!

00:13:11.981 --> 00:13:12.814
- [Rie] Okay.

00:13:12.814 --> 00:13:14.550
- And we have the make it fancy,

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:15.900
like the full-out version.
(Rie laughs)

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.961
- Okay, I like the second one,

00:13:17.961 --> 00:13:19.040
but I don't think I can do it.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:20.940
- So you go diagonal, all the way up.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:21.773
- Uh-huh.

00:13:21.773 --> 00:13:23.290
- And then here.
Uh-huh.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.123
- And then down.

00:13:24.123 --> 00:13:25.060
- Okay.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.250
- Or we could even just go,

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.680
up and down.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.270
- Okay, okay.
Yes, yes!

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.860
- [Rie and Jordyn] Make it fancy!

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.229
- Did I do that? (laughs)

00:13:32.229 --> 00:13:34.979
(cheerful music)

